Local testnet browser smoke summary
Checked: 2026-07-10
Origin: http://localhost:3000 (local-only, not launch evidence)

PASS: desktop and mobile hub shells, manual/auto-miner numeric typography, mounted
pool-chart line, desktop/mobile Privy wallet selector options, auto-miner local
persistence, chat/profile modal, and Analytics, Safety Pool, Leaderboards,
White Paper, FAQ, and Hub navigation.

Tile selection reached a valid closed/resolving-epoch state after 45,226 ms; the
UI remained responsive and surfaced the locked state rather than silently failing.

This smoke did not connect a signed Privy wallet and did not submit a transaction.
It is runtime/UI evidence only, not signed wallet recovery or final testnet proof.

Signed desktop Privy recovery addendum (2026-07-10, local-only): PASS.
After a production-server restart and browser reload, the embedded wallet returned
to Active within 6 seconds; LOGIN remained absent and the auto-miner controls were
available. This does not cover mobile browser, wrong-network, rejection, pending,
revert, tab-close, or route-remount recovery states.

Signed desktop recovery follow-up (reviewed 2026-07-10T20:52:09.046Z): PASS.
- Hub -> Analytics -> Hub preserved the Active embedded wallet.
- Closing the temporary LORE tab, opening a new tab, and a full reload each restored
  Active without LOGIN; the grid and controls returned with zero console errors.
- After an intentionally cancelled MetaMask login attempt, closing the Privy modal
  restored Login / Connect without reloading. A subsequent approved MetaMask login
  restored the Active Privy session.
- A signed 1 LINEA Privy bet entered a disabled pending state, then confirmed and
  cleared selection without duplicate submission. Epoch 1996, tile 1, block
  30767779, tx 0x270d688ae535270e2ccc02f18b59f0d3deaef1ed783dfb3b11183a3ab4868d50.

Local failure-state UI follow-up (reviewed 2026-07-10T20:52:09.046Z): PASS.
Extended browser smoke rendered RPC-offline retry wait, Recovery queued,
RESUME PENDING, Session Expired guidance, and recovery-state cleanup on desktop;
the complete desktop/mobile smoke also passed wallet selectors, mounted pool chart,
numeric typography, persistence, navigation, chat, and mobile layout.

Wrong-network limitation: a pre-fix Ethereum Sepolia top-up attempt exposed an
unbounded network-switch wait. The switch and chain checks are now bounded and
cannot launch a duplicate fallback after rejection/timeout, but a signed post-fix
MetaMask rejection is not yet recorded. A true mobile-device session and a signed
reverted transaction are also still missing; responsive viewport checks do not
claim either result.

Post-fix wrong-network follow-up (reviewed 2026-07-10T21:22:47.693Z): PARTIAL.
With MetaMask on Ethereum Sepolia, a 0.000001 ETH top-up switched to Linea Sepolia
and opened the expected transaction confirmation to the embedded Privy address.
MetaMask displayed two queued confirmations because the top-up button was clicked
twice explicitly. A synchronous shared wallet-transfer lock was then added so rapid
duplicate clicks cannot submit a second ETH/LINEA deposit or withdrawal before the
loading-state rerender. Transaction rejection or settlement was not yet recorded.

